---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { site, pillars } from "../data/site.js";

const title = "Tax Advisory for Business Owners & Equity | Advisant";
const description =
  "Employer equity planning, tax strategy for business owners, and family office services from enrolled agents in Metro Detroit and Denver.";
const equity = pillars[0], owners = pillars[1];

const schema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "Service",
  "@id": `${site.domain}/tax-advisory/#service`,
  name: "Tax Advisory for Business Owners and Equity Holders",
  description: "Employer equity planning, entity and compensation strategy, and year-end tax planning for business owners and equity holders.",
  provider: { "@id": `${site.domain}/#organization` },
  areaServed: [
    { "@type": "State", name: "Michigan" },
    { "@type": "State", name: "Colorado" },
  ],
};
---
<Base title={title} description={description} path="/tax-advisory/" schema={schema}>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="hero__grid">
        <div>
          <p class="formline formline--onDark">Advisory</p>
          <h1>Most tax advice arrives too late to matter.</h1>
          <p>
            By the time a return is being prepared, the decisions that moved the number were
            made months earlier — the exercise, the election, the distribution, the sale. We
            work on the side of that line where choices still exist.
          </p>
          <div class="hero__actions">
            <a class="btn" href="/contact/">New client application</a>
            <a class="btn btn--ghost" href="/family-office/">Family office services</a>
          </div>
        </div>
        <aside class="credential">
          <div class="credential__seal" aria-hidden="true">EA</div>
          <h2>Planning first, filing second.</h2>
          <p>
            Compliance is table stakes and we do it well. It is not why owners and equity
            holders hire us.
          </p>
          <dl>
            <dt>Focus</dt><dd>Owners, equity, families</dd>
            <dt>Cadence</dt><dd>Year-round, not seasonal</dd>
            <dt>Credential</dt><dd>Enrolled Agent (IRS)</dd>
          </dl>
        </aside>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band" id={equity.slug}>
    <div class="wrap split">
      <div class="prose">
        <p class="formline">Employer equity</p>
        <h2>{equity.title}</h2>
        <p>{equity.lede}</p>
        <p>
          Equity compensation punishes people who wait. The alternative minimum tax on an
          incentive stock option exercise is calculated on a spread the holder never received
          in cash. An 83(b) election is worthless on day 31. Qualified small business stock
          requires facts that must be true at issuance, not assembled at sale. None of these
          are fixable at filing.
        </p>
        <p>
          We model exercises against your full picture — other income, state residency,
          expected liquidity — and tell you what a given decision costs before you make it.
          Where a client is holding options through a company transaction, we work alongside
          their attorney rather than reacting to the closing documents afterward.
        </p>
        <h3>What this covers</h3>
        <ul>{equity.points.map((x) => <li>{x}</li>)}</ul>
      </div>
      <aside class="facts">
        <p class="formline">Common triggers</p>
        <ul style="list-style:none;margin:0;padding:0;font-size:.95rem">
          <li style="padding:.6rem 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule)">A first grant, or a grant you have not exercised</li>
          <li style="padding:.6rem 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule)">A tender offer or secondary sale</li>
          <li style="padding:.6rem 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule)">Leaving a company with vested options</li>
          <li style="padding:.6rem 0">An AMT bill you did not see coming</li>
        </ul>
        <a class="btn" href="/contact/">Start a conversation</a>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band band--sunk" id={owners.slug}>
    <div class="wrap split">
      <div class="prose">
        <p class="formline">Business owners</p>
        <h2>{owners.title}</h2>
        <p>{owners.lede}</p>
        <p>
          The questions owners actually face are structural. Whether the entity is still the
          right one. Whether the salary is defensible. Whether a retirement plan could absorb
          far more than it currently does. Whether the state election helps this owner group
          or only some of it. Whether the business is being run in a way that a buyer will pay
          for in three years.
        </p>
        <p>
          These are not filing-season questions and they cannot be answered from a completed
          return. We work through them on a calendar that matches when the decisions are
          actually made — which for most of them is well before December.
        </p>
        <h3>What this covers</h3>
        <ul>{owners.points.map((x) => <li>{x}</li>)}</ul>
        <p>
          If a sale is in view, the structural work starts earlier still — see
          <a href="/business-exit-tax-planning/"> business exit tax planning</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
      <aside class="facts">
        <p class="formline">Common triggers</p>
        <ul style="list-style:none;margin:0;padding:0;font-size:.95rem">
          <li style="padding:.6rem 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule)">Profit that has outgrown the current structure</li>
          <li style="padding:.6rem 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule)">Hiring in a second or third state</li>
          <li style="padding:.6rem 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule)">Bringing on or buying out a partner</li>
          <li style="padding:.6rem 0">A sale within the next three to five years</li>
        </ul>
        <a class="btn" href="/contact/">Start a conversation</a>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band">
    <div class="wrap measure">
      <p class="formline">Also</p>
      <h2>Family office services</h2>
      <p>
        For families running more than one entity, a trust structure, or a philanthropic
        vehicle, we hold the whole picture rather than a slice of it.
      </p>
      <p style="margin-top:1.5rem"><a class="btn" href="/family-office/">Family office services</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
